  "created_at": "2026-08-26T16:34:10Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-26T16:34:10Z",
  "body": "\n\nOther than the confusing/misleading documentation; there's also several lapses that cost real bugs, exhibit:\nneither `./docs/building` or the `makefile` document/expose the `--portable` option to not require the sed hack\n```\n\t\t_echo \"* Cloning $CROSS_LIBC_DLOPEN_REPO...\"\n\t\trm -rf \"$CLD_SRC\"\n\t\tgit clone \"$CROSS_LIBC_DLOPEN_REPO\" \"$CLD_SRC\" && (\n\t\t\tcd \"$CLD_SRC\"/src\n\t\t\t# -fcf-protection=full is not supported on all gcc targets\n\t\t\t# and has no functional benefit so it is removed\n\t\t\tsed -i -e 's/ -fcf-protection=full//' Makefile\n\t\t\tmake\n\t\t)\n```\n\nuseable per: https://github.com/pkgforge-dev/cross-libc-dlopen/blob/main/scripts/build.sh#L67\n```\n--portable)  VARIANT=portable; EXTRA_CFLAGS=-DCLD_STRICT_ENV; NO_CET=1; shift ;;\n```\n\nFurthermore, one shouldn't need to use the build script, they should be able to do `make portable` & that should be sufficient\n\nDownstream has no idea it even exists without reading actual code/comments, yet another oversight & lack of actually useful & clear documentation (https://github.com/pkgforge-dev/cross-libc-dlopen/pull/12)",
