  "updated_at": "2026-08-26T16:40:05Z",
  "body": "This is not only limited to the Readme, see https://github.com/pkgforge-dev/cross-libc-dlopen/issues/13\r\nAnd from discord conversation:\r\n> glibc is backwards compatible\r\n> you will always be able to dlopen a library that was built againts an older glibc than the one you ship, this is how we have\r\n> always been able to use the host nvidia driver before, because nvidia makes sure to release linking againts super old versions of glibc always\r\n> did you let the AI know about old kernels, linuxulator, apparmor, selinux?\r\n> because those things might give us problem with the fcf flag\r\n> do you remember the many problems Max had with UPXed binaries not being able to run on some systems?\r\n> so some terrible hallucination happened here\r\n\r\nThe whole documentation including userfacing buildscripts/makefiles need a major overhaul.\r\nThey are meant to be read by humans with not much context & it doesn't help when AI hallucinates or makes contradictory misleading claims.\r\nThis is simply unacceptable & violates ./docs/conventions",
