  "created_at": "2026-08-26T18:11:52Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-26T18:11:52Z",
  "body": "@QaidVoid I think we should just never state anything about the glibc version this requires to be built on, this just causes confusion.\r\n\r\nglibc has backwards compat, a library built with glibc 2.17 will work with all future versions of glibc.\r\n\r\nThat means we can build and preload this shim in archlinux and we will be able to dlopen libs from a glibc 2.17 host without problem, this is a feature of glibc already.\r\n\r\nWhat the shim solves is that we will be able to dlopen libs of newer glibc versions in the future.",
